ble international partners. Ethiopia is landlocked, but, according to Hussein, is fully dependent on the Red Sea for maritime trade. The Bab el-Mandeb Strait connects the Red Sea with the Gulf of Aden and is an important route for vessels traveling between Asia, the Suez Canal, and Europe. More current news is available on the UA.News Telegram channel Telegram . Participants’ positions and dispute with Eritrea UN Secretary-General’s Special Envoy for the Horn of Africa Guang Cong described the situation in the region as a polycrisis. According to him, the wars in Sudan, South Sudan, and Somalia, as well as threats to shipping in the Red Sea, are closely interconnected. The envoys of Germany and France also stressed the need to strengthen multilateral cooperation and support peace initiatives led by countries in the region, as well as economic integration. During the discussion, Ethiopian Prime Minister’s adviser for East Africa Getachew Reda said that Eritrea continues actions that fuel the crisis. Earlier, Eritrea’s Ministry of Foreign Affairs rejected Addis Ababa’s accusations that Eritrean troops had crossed into Ethiopian territory. Read us on Download our app RELATED MATERIALS News Around the World President Lula’s campaign to ask for voting extension — The Rio Times News Around the World Flávio Bolsonaro led in unofficial overseas vote count — The Rio Times News Around the World Saudi Arabia signs statement calling Israel a source of instability — Jerusalem Post News Around the World Cooper says Strait of Hormuz is free of Iranian mines — Jerusalem Post News Around the World IDF wounds but does not detain Palestinian suspected of attempted ramming near Hebron — Jerusalem Post News Around the World PM Netanyahu warns of risk of attacks before Israel’s elections — Asharq Al-Awsat News Around the World Brazilian court expects runoff result by 21:00 in Brasília — The Rio Times × World Ukraine Kyiv Polytics Business Technologies Sport proLife Use of materials from 